1
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Sharpe's Rifles is a war, adventure, tv movie film directed by Tom Clegg.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
During the Peninsular War in Spain against the French, Sergeant Richard Sharpe saves the life of
Arthur Wellesley, the future Duke of Wellington and is promoted to Lieutenant.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
In order to pay the troops Wellesley needs a money draft from the banker Rothschild, but fears he
has been captured by the French and sends Sharpe behind enemy lines to find him.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Sharpe is given command of a platoon of crack riflemen, led by the surly Irishman Harper and
including Hagman and Harris, who resent Sharpe as not being a 'proper officer'.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Richard Sharpe, played by Sean Bean.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Major Michael Hogan, played by Brian Cox.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Patrick Harper, played by Daragh O'Malley.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Comandante Teresa Moreno, played by Assumpta Serna.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Sir Arthur Wellesley, played by David Troughton.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Rifleman Daniel Hagman, played by John Tams.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Sharpe's Rifles is the first of the Sharpe television dramas, based
on Bernard Cornwell's 1988 novel of the same name.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Shown on ITV in 1993, the adaptation stars Sean Bean,
Daragh O'Malley and Assumpta Serna.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It began a long series of successful and critically
acclaimed television adaptations of the novels.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The drama tells the story of Richard Sharpe, an
ambitious and hardened soldier from Yorkshire.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The story follows the exploits of Sharpe and his band of chosen men
through Spain after they survive an ambush by French cavalry.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Filming took place in the Crimea, Portugal and England, during which Paul McGann who was the original actor
cast for the role of Richard Sharpe, broke his leg and was quickly replaced with Sean Bean.
